                <pb facs="0572" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.1D1/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-15T17:00:00-05:00">November 15, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>379. Your 523, November 13, 7 p.m. Department approves the first sentence of your
                    proposed statement but feels that the second sentence thereof should be omitted.
                    Department prefers to avoid any suggestion which might lead to the conclusion
                    that a Convention excepting the individual States would be more acceptable to
                    this Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
